{"event_type":"review","id":"092c2d8bb389521fa71f4f8d6beacda7ba9b4c13f114c97d8385d2b1a5bb125f","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T19:30:06Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/86663222dfa0ae72f2e5fca919555fcca5fac776d1124cbb3581903bc8b99a04","sha256":"86663222dfa0ae72f2e5fca919555fcca5fac776d1124cbb3581903bc8b99a04"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b8502ed1405a5e2306b55050a6c342cdda186662ad81f9c7dc07679d21efd04c","sha256":"b8502ed1405a5e2306b55050a6c342cdda186662ad81f9c7dc07679d21efd04c"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/be2bb2378bc6419ea69e06e15a4a53bf8a330f079b0b1ed725540be45002cb95","sha256":"be2bb2378bc6419ea69e06e15a4a53bf8a330f079b0b1ed725540be45002cb95"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/07b5a61208bb2891872f41974eb81a992d9d926cd84514743caf264ff5d61380","sha256":"07b5a61208bb2891872f41974eb81a992d9d926cd84514743caf264ff5d61380"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/220d3dad8e0a8c5e97f6c541c48269d26ce5b9e8b67af4469eec63df1496cee4","sha256":"220d3dad8e0a8c5e97f6c541c48269d26ce5b9e8b67af4469eec63df1496cee4"}],"attempt_id":"6c89fa3d43226209f95c57da84e99c1e6cd03b9e5e2623b5fe9f94bda1b54e27:0:1","base":"b14494a5b716a7b1e1a6a888c527ddd1f7458cc2","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"f49d7963b70101cd753b75a8894d7cb7efcb817b","body":"**Stop serializing the version 2 fixture with `serializeDevLedger`.**\n\n`serializeDevLedger` throws for any ledger whose `version` is not `DEV_LEDGER_VERSION` (3). The `fixture()` ledger declares `version: 2`, and `legacy` copies that value. Both calls at lines 166 and 168 therefore throw `cannot serialize ledger version 2` before any `expect` runs, so the test fails on every run.\n\nThe test also checks the wrong path. Version 2 support means v2 JSON can be read. It does not mean v2 ledgers can be written. Parse the raw v2 JSON instead. Call `serializeDevLedger` only on a version 3 copy when a write is needed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  expect(parseDevLedger(serializeDevLedger(f.ledger))).toEqual(f.ledger);\n-  const legacy = { ...f.ledger, records: [cycleRecord()] };\n-  expect(parseDevLedger(serializeDevLedger(legacy))).toEqual(legacy);\n+  expect(parseDevLedger(JSON.stringify(f.ledger))).toEqual(f.ledger);\n+  const legacy = { ...f.ledger, records: [cycleRecord()] };\n+  expect(parseDevLedger(JSON.stringify(legacy))).toEqual(legacy);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"5b14fe95291cf98a5784bad0d22919dd9f93cc4d12362a36eb9551bac6ccae2a","intervals":[],"path":"test/ops/dev/deferredLedger.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Stop serializing the version 2 fixture with `serializeDevLedger`."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"28d22ad3ad526a01aef85a62fb12a074a0f955a2","body":"**Preserve all ledger finding fields when rebuilding CodeRabbit findings.**\n\nLedger findings can include `line`, `rule`, `evidence`, and `evidenceV1`, but `src/ops/review/run.ts:319-331` omits them. `sameFindingContent` compares these fields. The omitted fields therefore make an unchanged finding fail the content check, so its fixed or rejected disposition can be discarded and the finding can return to `open`.\n\nThe initial lookup is ID-only, but the downstream Q17b path performs the content check. The issue is the lost metadata, not that a changed same-ID finding ultimately inherits a disposition.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n                     text: finding.excerpt ?? '',\n                     ...(finding.fileName !== undefined ? { file: finding.fileName } : {}),\n+                    ...(finding.line !== undefined ? { line: finding.line } : {}),\n+                    ...(finding.rule !== undefined ? { rule: finding.rule } : {}),\n+                    ...(finding.evidence !== undefined ? { evidence: finding.evidence } : {}),\n+                    ...(finding.evidenceV1 !== undefined ? { evidenceV1: finding.evidenceV1 } : {}),\n                     status: disposition?.action ?? 'open',\n```\n\n</details>","id":"23c2067103ceec25d2f2bf47707f7a67c6127529debb21294b7bc02a49d42ede","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/run.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Preserve all ledger finding fields when rebuilding CodeRabbit findings."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"28d22ad3ad526a01aef85a62fb12a074a0f955a2","body":"**Map evidence-preparation failures to a failed result.**\n\n`readBlob` at `src/ops/review/run.ts:617` awaits `effects.runCommand` without a catch. Spawn faults and `maxBuffer` errors reject this promise. The same applies to the `runCommand` and `readWorktreeFile` awaits in `loadEvidencePaths` at lines 659 and 667.\n\nThe enclosing `execute` has cleanup in `finally`, but no catch. The public `review.run` registry returns `makeReviewRun` directly, and the agent-review boundary also has cleanup in `finally` without converting these rejections. Catch the evidence-preparation and evidence-loading failures at the operation boundary and return `{ status: 'failed', error }`. Treat only a normal non-zero `git show` exit as missing content; do not convert rejected commands into `undefined`.","id":"aef7dba26cb42569891fe659950748587b55a751cfcf74636422d6a8fec7d4d6","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/run.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Map evidence-preparation failures to a failed result."}],"head":"96679a92b1eeea05a09908dae9087c1890b8028e","head_tree":"caf2bd1c0f6a76b490442f34307539ee3268e814","input_scope":[{"blob":"30942f01d0fce03e421b3e033bce798dda45ea1e","intervals":[[8,28],[42,42],[47,48],[53,53]],"path":"docs/current-contract-and-backlog.md"},{"blob":"f5d62267b1f632c077d13a39c32576d8fb18fe15","interval